From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:08:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 58/61] NNS.stack: remove dead and duplicated code; drop unused
 NNS_mreg_reduce_cpp

- Univariate "all" final fit: .fit_univariate_raw(...) was fitted and
  immediately overwritten by a second NNS.reg fit (a wasted full fit).
- Multivariate "all" final fit: .nns_mreg_prepare_model was re-run on
  the full data only to count RPM rows; take nrow() of the RPM of the
  final NNS.reg fit instead (same model, same order, noise.reduction
  "off").
- probability.threshold <- if (is_class) 0.5 else 0.5 -> 0.5.
- src/table_ops.cpp: NNS_mreg_reduce_cpp was exported but never called,
  and its reducer codes (0 gravity, 1 mean, 2 median, 3 mode)
  contradict the reducer.code used for NNS_mreg_setup_cpp (mean 0,
  median 1, mode 2, off 3), so wiring it in would silently swap
  reducers. The file only held that function and is deleted;
  RcppExports regenerated with Rcpp::compileAttributes.

Results are unchanged: NNS.stack (univariate and multivariate Method 1
with ALL selected, n.best 156; default stack with pred.int; iris CLASS),
NNS.boost on iris and NNS.reg(noise.reduction = "mode") are identical()
before and after.
